1
00:00:00,310 --> 00:00:02,560
If your knee replacement
still hurts

2
00:00:02,560 --> 00:00:05,230
and the X-ray keeps coming
back fine,

3
00:00:05,230 --> 00:00:06,300
don't accept that.

4
00:00:06,520 --> 00:00:08,100
I've been cleaning hotel
rooms

5
00:00:08,100 --> 00:00:09,320
for thirty years.

6
00:00:10,070 --> 00:00:11,440
Kneeling by the tub

7
00:00:11,440 --> 00:00:12,600
and making beds,

8
00:00:12,600 --> 00:00:13,850
room after room.

9
00:00:14,160 --> 00:00:15,140
I had my right knee

10
00:00:15,140 --> 00:00:17,000
replaced two years ago.

11
00:00:17,170 --> 00:00:18,940
It has hurt every day
since.

12
00:00:19,640 --> 00:00:21,000
Not surgery pain.

13
00:00:21,400 --> 00:00:22,800
I know what that felt
like,

14
00:00:22,800 --> 00:00:23,750
and it went away.

15
00:00:24,310 --> 00:00:25,360
This is different.

16
00:00:25,570 --> 00:00:26,260
Tight.

17
00:00:26,400 --> 00:00:27,120
Full.

18
00:00:27,710 --> 00:00:28,530
Like a band around

19
00:00:28,530 --> 00:00:30,400
the joint that never
loosens.

20
00:00:30,770 --> 00:00:31,730
And for two years I've

21
00:00:31,730 --> 00:00:33,120
been told the same thing.

22
00:00:33,500 --> 00:00:34,460
Give it time.

23
00:00:34,670 --> 00:00:36,430
At six weeks it was
swelling,

24
00:00:36,430 --> 00:00:37,710
and swelling is normal.

25
00:00:37,930 --> 00:00:39,350
At three months,

26
00:00:39,350 --> 00:00:40,320
give it six.

27
00:00:40,510 --> 00:00:41,610
At six months,

28
00:00:41,610 --> 00:00:43,250
some knees take a full
year.

29
00:00:43,820 --> 00:00:44,610
At a year,

30
00:00:44,610 --> 00:00:46,440
eighteen months isn't
unusual.

31
00:00:46,740 --> 00:00:48,040
And I didn't just wait.

32
00:00:48,350 --> 00:00:49,550
We went down the list.

33
00:00:49,590 --> 00:00:50,860
More physical therapy.

34
00:00:50,980 --> 00:00:51,730
Every session,

35
00:00:51,730 --> 00:00:53,380
every exercise at home.

36
00:00:53,650 --> 00:00:54,710
I got stronger.

37
00:00:54,940 --> 00:00:56,430
The tightness never moved.

38
00:00:56,490 --> 00:00:57,940
The pain pills helped,

39
00:00:57,940 --> 00:00:59,230
and that was the problem.

40
00:00:59,610 --> 00:01:01,500
I'm already on enough
every morning,

41
00:01:01,500 --> 00:01:02,460
and nobody could tell me

42
00:01:02,460 --> 00:01:03,680
when I'd get to stop.

43
00:01:03,980 --> 00:01:05,610
Then a nerve block.

44
00:01:05,670 --> 00:01:07,550
Then talk of burning the
nerve.

45
00:01:08,240 --> 00:01:09,550
And after that, a second

46
00:01:09,550 --> 00:01:10,720
operation to go back

47
00:01:10,720 --> 00:01:12,150
in and do it over.

48
00:01:12,510 --> 00:01:13,510
I said no.

49
00:01:13,700 --> 00:01:15,810
Every morning I stepped
out of bed

50
00:01:15,810 --> 00:01:16,740
and my knee felt like

51
00:01:16,740 --> 00:01:18,470
a band was wrapped around
it,

52
00:01:18,470 --> 00:01:20,740
tightening every inch I
tried to straighten.

53
00:01:20,890 --> 00:01:22,300
Every morning I took
something

54
00:01:22,300 --> 00:01:24,010
for it and went to work.

55
00:01:24,080 --> 00:01:25,230
Couldn't kneel to tuck

56
00:01:25,230 --> 00:01:26,470
in a sheet without
grabbing

57
00:01:26,470 --> 00:01:27,860
the bed to get back up,

58
00:01:27,860 --> 00:01:29,140
couldn't do the stairs,

59
00:01:29,140 --> 00:01:30,290
couldn't stand at the
counter

60
00:01:30,290 --> 00:01:31,850
long enough to finish
dinner,

61
00:01:31,850 --> 00:01:33,540
couldn't sit through my
granddaughter's game

62
00:01:33,540 --> 00:01:35,420
without shifting every two
minutes.

63
00:01:35,610 --> 00:01:37,030
It woke me at night,

64
00:01:37,030 --> 00:01:39,040
and it turned ordinary
things,

65
00:01:39,040 --> 00:01:40,270
like getting in the car

66
00:01:40,270 --> 00:01:41,610
or up off the couch,

67
00:01:41,610 --> 00:01:42,710
into a decision.

68
00:01:43,340 --> 00:01:44,810
I didn't know how many
more rooms

69
00:01:44,810 --> 00:01:45,950
I had left in me.

70
00:01:46,090 --> 00:01:47,410
After a long and serious

71
00:01:47,410 --> 00:01:48,810
talk with my husband,

72
00:01:48,810 --> 00:01:50,510
I went back in one more
time.

73
00:01:50,730 --> 00:01:51,680
That was the fourth set

74
00:01:51,680 --> 00:01:53,100
of X-rays on this knee.

75
00:01:53,390 --> 00:01:54,950
And like the three before
it,

76
00:01:54,950 --> 00:01:56,960
the answer was everything
looks great.

77
00:01:57,150 --> 00:01:59,340
No loosening, no
infection,

78
00:01:59,340 --> 00:02:00,280
nothing wrong.

79
00:02:00,470 --> 00:02:01,380
Only this time there

80
00:02:01,380 --> 00:02:02,570
was no new number.

81
00:02:02,800 --> 00:02:04,960
Nobody said give it
another six months.

82
00:02:05,130 --> 00:02:06,560
There was nothing left to
give it.

83
00:02:07,100 --> 00:02:07,910
I sat in the parking

84
00:02:07,910 --> 00:02:08,980
lot for a while.

85
00:02:09,110 --> 00:02:10,830
Okay, I thought.

86
00:02:10,930 --> 00:02:12,330
Then explain this.

87
00:02:12,460 --> 00:02:14,440
Anyway, a couple of months
back,

88
00:02:14,440 --> 00:02:15,950
I hit my breaking point.

89
00:02:16,140 --> 00:02:18,090
It was around 2:30 in the
morning.

90
00:02:19,130 --> 00:02:21,020
I had a whole floor of
rooms

91
00:02:21,020 --> 00:02:22,060
waiting at eight.

92
00:02:22,140 --> 00:02:23,980
Everyone in the house was
asleep

93
00:02:23,980 --> 00:02:25,590
and I was downstairs in
the recliner

94
00:02:25,590 --> 00:02:27,290
with my leg up,

95
00:02:27,290 --> 00:02:28,880
trying to find any angle
where

96
00:02:28,880 --> 00:02:30,030
it didn't feel like
something

97
00:02:30,030 --> 00:02:32,140
was wrapped around my knee
and tightening.

98
00:02:32,360 --> 00:02:34,790
My husband didn't know I'd
come downstairs.

99
00:02:34,890 --> 00:02:36,640
By then I'd stopped
telling him.

100
00:02:36,770 --> 00:02:38,390
And I just thought,

101
00:02:38,390 --> 00:02:40,160
is this really my life
now?

102
00:02:40,490 --> 00:02:42,010
I can't live like this.

103
00:02:42,140 --> 00:02:43,770
So I made myself a
promise.

104
00:02:44,080 --> 00:02:44,990
I wouldn't go a day

105
00:02:44,990 --> 00:02:46,610
without looking for an
answer.

106
00:02:46,740 --> 00:02:48,020
And when I found one,

107
00:02:48,020 --> 00:02:49,090
I'd share it with everyone

108
00:02:49,090 --> 00:02:50,500
going through the same
thing.

109
00:02:50,580 --> 00:02:52,600
So I got my laptop out

110
00:02:52,600 --> 00:02:53,640
and went looking.

111
00:02:53,980 --> 00:02:55,200
Not for a product.

112
00:02:56,120 --> 00:02:57,420
For an explanation.

113
00:02:57,620 --> 00:02:59,220
Mayo Clinic forums,

114
00:02:59,220 --> 00:03:01,380
the knee replacement group
on Facebook,

115
00:03:01,380 --> 00:03:02,680
doctor videos,

116
00:03:02,680 --> 00:03:04,220
medical animations.

117
00:03:04,470 --> 00:03:05,380
And that's when I found

118
00:03:05,380 --> 00:03:07,380
a video from a physical
therapist

119
00:03:07,380 --> 00:03:07,990
named Dr.

120
00:03:08,030 --> 00:03:10,240
Steven Salinger, whose own
wife

121
00:03:10,240 --> 00:03:12,080
had been through exactly
this.

122
00:03:12,270 --> 00:03:13,730
But before I say anything
else,

123
00:03:13,730 --> 00:03:15,140
I want to be straight with
you.

124
00:03:15,490 --> 00:03:17,320
You've already had
something work fast.

125
00:03:17,820 --> 00:03:18,660
The ice.

126
00:03:18,870 --> 00:03:20,360
The first week of a new
pill.

127
00:03:20,860 --> 00:03:22,510
The good day after a
session.

128
00:03:22,820 --> 00:03:23,890
Then it wore off.

129
00:03:24,080 --> 00:03:25,880
That's the part nobody
warns you about.

130
00:03:26,100 --> 00:03:28,010
Fast relief isn't relief.

131
00:03:28,120 --> 00:03:29,150
It's a preview.

132
00:03:29,300 --> 00:03:30,160
So I'm not going to tell

133
00:03:30,160 --> 00:03:31,470
you this works fast.

134
00:03:31,600 --> 00:03:32,370
It doesn't.

135
00:03:32,500 --> 00:03:34,290
But if you're willing to
be patient,

136
00:03:34,290 --> 00:03:35,040
and to look at what's

137
00:03:35,040 --> 00:03:36,380
going on around your new
knee

138
00:03:36,380 --> 00:03:37,910
instead of inside it,
there

139
00:03:37,910 --> 00:03:39,760
is a real reason it still
hurts.

140
00:03:39,890 --> 00:03:41,660
And something you can do
about it.

141
00:03:42,290 --> 00:03:44,070
Let me explain what he
said,

142
00:03:44,070 --> 00:03:45,390
because this is what
changed

143
00:03:45,390 --> 00:03:46,680
everything for me.

144
00:03:47,000 --> 00:03:48,770
He started with the
basics.

145
00:03:48,860 --> 00:03:50,280
A knee replacement takes
out

146
00:03:50,280 --> 00:03:52,000
the worn joint surfaces

147
00:03:52,000 --> 00:03:53,870
and puts in metal and
plastic.

148
00:03:53,950 --> 00:03:55,710
That's what stops the
arthritis pain

149
00:03:55,710 --> 00:03:57,490
you had before the
operation.

150
00:03:57,710 --> 00:03:59,320
That part I already knew.

151
00:03:59,720 --> 00:04:01,080
But then he explained
something

152
00:04:01,080 --> 00:04:02,570
nobody had ever told me.

153
00:04:02,680 --> 00:04:03,580
He said,

154
00:04:03,580 --> 00:04:04,890
think about a swollen foot

155
00:04:04,890 --> 00:04:06,020
inside a shoe.

156
00:04:06,180 --> 00:04:07,570
The shoe didn't shrink.

157
00:04:07,690 --> 00:04:09,670
Your foot is taking up
more room,

158
00:04:09,670 --> 00:04:11,150
so everything feels
cramped

159
00:04:11,150 --> 00:04:12,640
and tight and squeezed.

160
00:04:12,880 --> 00:04:13,800
Your new knee sits

161
00:04:13,800 --> 00:04:15,310
in a limited space with
living

162
00:04:15,310 --> 00:04:16,940
tissue packed all around
it.

163
00:04:17,340 --> 00:04:19,010
To put that knee in, the
surgeon

164
00:04:19,010 --> 00:04:20,690
had to work through that
tissue.

165
00:04:20,900 --> 00:04:23,270
Afterwards it gets
inflamed and swollen.

166
00:04:23,400 --> 00:04:24,910
At first that's normal.

167
00:04:25,000 --> 00:04:26,370
But in some people

168
00:04:26,370 --> 00:04:27,810
that swelling can stay
switched

169
00:04:27,810 --> 00:04:29,720
on far longer than
expected.

170
00:04:30,510 --> 00:04:32,110
And swollen tissue takes
up more

171
00:04:32,110 --> 00:04:33,920
room than calm tissue
does.

172
00:04:34,040 --> 00:04:35,210
So when you bend,

173
00:04:35,210 --> 00:04:36,950
that tissue gets
compressed.

174
00:04:37,110 --> 00:04:37,940
When you straighten,

175
00:04:37,940 --> 00:04:39,270
it gets pulled tight.

176
00:04:39,530 --> 00:04:40,590
That's the band.

177
00:04:40,730 --> 00:04:42,940
That's the ache that never
quite leaves.

178
00:04:43,200 --> 00:04:44,040
And you start being

179
00:04:44,040 --> 00:04:45,490
the one who says,

180
00:04:45,490 --> 00:04:46,600
you go ahead.

181
00:04:46,740 --> 00:04:47,750
I'll stay here.

182
00:04:47,920 --> 00:04:49,420
And that's exactly why so
much

183
00:04:49,420 --> 00:04:51,120
of what I'd tried hadn't
worked.

184
00:04:51,380 --> 00:04:53,410
Physical therapy
strengthens the muscles

185
00:04:53,410 --> 00:04:54,340
around the knee.

186
00:04:55,100 --> 00:04:56,230
Worth doing,

187
00:04:56,230 --> 00:04:57,240
and I'd done it.

188
00:04:57,730 --> 00:04:59,010
It does nothing about
tissue

189
00:04:59,010 --> 00:05:00,130
taking up room.

190
00:05:00,440 --> 00:05:01,680
A nerve block quiets

191
00:05:01,680 --> 00:05:03,510
the nerve carrying the
signal.

192
00:05:03,620 --> 00:05:05,510
It doesn't touch what's
generating it.

193
00:05:06,180 --> 00:05:07,690
But when that irritated
tissue

194
00:05:07,690 --> 00:05:09,440
finally calms down,

195
00:05:09,440 --> 00:05:11,020
it holds less fluid,

196
00:05:11,020 --> 00:05:12,590
and it takes up less room.

197
00:05:13,000 --> 00:05:14,280
Less room taken up means

198
00:05:14,280 --> 00:05:16,240
less pressure squeezing
the joint.

199
00:05:16,530 --> 00:05:18,180
That's what takes the
pressure off.

200
00:05:18,360 --> 00:05:19,600
After two years of this,

201
00:05:19,600 --> 00:05:21,100
it finally made sense.

202
00:05:21,260 --> 00:05:23,130
The problem was never the
new knee.

203
00:05:23,370 --> 00:05:25,340
It was the tissue crowded
around it.

204
00:05:25,510 --> 00:05:27,070
He calls it the squeeze.

205
00:05:27,340 --> 00:05:29,780
Once you've felt it,
that's the word.

206
00:05:29,880 --> 00:05:31,050
I'd bought knee sleeves,

207
00:05:31,050 --> 00:05:32,460
compression braces,

208
00:05:32,460 --> 00:05:34,940
a kneeling pad for work,
creams,

209
00:05:34,940 --> 00:05:36,740
half of Amazon really,

210
00:05:36,740 --> 00:05:37,960
and all any of it gave

211
00:05:37,960 --> 00:05:38,990
me was an hour.

212
00:05:39,190 --> 00:05:40,250
I even looked at going

213
00:05:40,250 --> 00:05:42,140
to a clinic for the light
therapy.

214
00:05:42,260 --> 00:05:43,720
But at $200 a session

215
00:05:43,720 --> 00:05:45,350
with nothing covered by
insurance,

216
00:05:45,350 --> 00:05:46,640
that was a quick no.

217
00:05:46,960 --> 00:05:47,860
Then one night I went

218
00:05:47,860 --> 00:05:49,120
back to that knee
replacement

219
00:05:49,120 --> 00:05:50,600
group and actually read
it.

220
00:05:50,790 --> 00:05:51,990
Thousands of people,

221
00:05:51,990 --> 00:05:53,470
years out from surgery,

222
00:05:53,470 --> 00:05:55,790
comparing notes on
stiffness and tightness

223
00:05:55,790 --> 00:05:57,140
nobody could explain.

224
00:05:57,330 --> 00:05:59,260
And no matter how far I
scrolled,

225
00:05:59,260 --> 00:06:00,880
the same thing kept coming
up.

226
00:06:01,020 --> 00:06:01,930
This one device,

227
00:06:01,930 --> 00:06:03,610
and people saying it was
the first

228
00:06:03,610 --> 00:06:04,960
thing that made a
difference.

229
00:06:05,310 --> 00:06:07,340
And before anyone jumps in
thinking,

230
00:06:07,340 --> 00:06:08,750
alright, here it comes,

231
00:06:08,750 --> 00:06:10,240
she's selling me
something,

232
00:06:10,240 --> 00:06:11,890
let me shut that down
right now.

233
00:06:12,070 --> 00:06:13,760
I'm only here because I
made myself

234
00:06:13,760 --> 00:06:16,060
a promise at 2:30 in the
morning

235
00:06:16,060 --> 00:06:17,090
that if I ever found

236
00:06:17,090 --> 00:06:18,260
something that helped,

237
00:06:18,260 --> 00:06:19,250
I'd say so.

238
00:06:19,710 --> 00:06:21,190
It's called the KenRelief

239
00:06:21,190 --> 00:06:22,670
Red Light Therapy Wrap.

240
00:06:23,350 --> 00:06:24,490
At first glance

241
00:06:24,490 --> 00:06:25,380
I didn't buy it.

242
00:06:25,620 --> 00:06:27,240
It looked like the cheap
knee sleeves

243
00:06:27,240 --> 00:06:29,240
off Amazon that did
nothing for me.

244
00:06:29,730 --> 00:06:31,710
But I went to their
website anyway,

245
00:06:31,710 --> 00:06:32,570
just to see what all

246
00:06:32,570 --> 00:06:33,680
the fuss was about.

247
00:06:33,940 --> 00:06:36,060
It's the same red light
therapy clinics

248
00:06:36,060 --> 00:06:38,610
charge $200 a session for,

249
00:06:38,610 --> 00:06:41,580
off machines that cost
fifty thousand dollars,

250
00:06:41,580 --> 00:06:42,490
in a wrap you plug

251
00:06:42,490 --> 00:06:43,800
into the wall at home.

252
00:06:43,850 --> 00:06:45,530
Two hundred and forty
lights.

253
00:06:45,690 --> 00:06:47,880
Red at 660 nanometers

254
00:06:47,880 --> 00:06:50,400
and near-infrared at 850,

255
00:06:50,400 --> 00:06:52,580
run together for the
strongest effect.

256
00:06:52,890 --> 00:06:54,490
Four strength levels.

257
00:06:54,640 --> 00:06:56,540
A five to thirty minute
timer.

258
00:06:57,190 --> 00:06:58,900
Then I saw the guarantee.

259
00:06:59,500 --> 00:07:00,540
Ninety days.

260
00:07:00,620 --> 00:07:02,990
Results or your money
back,

261
00:07:02,990 --> 00:07:04,200
no questions,

262
00:07:04,200 --> 00:07:05,450
no store credit,

263
00:07:05,450 --> 00:07:07,140
and you don't even send it
back.

264
00:07:07,500 --> 00:07:09,820
No physical therapist ever
gave me ninety

265
00:07:09,820 --> 00:07:11,020
days to change my mind.

266
00:07:11,060 --> 00:07:12,820
There wasn't much to lose,

267
00:07:12,820 --> 00:07:13,840
so I ordered it.

268
00:07:14,290 --> 00:07:15,870
Two of them, actually.

269
00:07:16,040 --> 00:07:17,700
Only the right knee was
replaced,

270
00:07:17,700 --> 00:07:19,450
but you favor the leg that
hurts,

271
00:07:19,450 --> 00:07:21,020
and I'd done it for two
years.

272
00:07:21,560 --> 00:07:23,480
The left one was carrying
the difference.

273
00:07:23,760 --> 00:07:24,500
When it came,

274
00:07:24,500 --> 00:07:26,810
I strapped it on expecting
nothing,

275
00:07:26,810 --> 00:07:28,020
because I'd been let down
too

276
00:07:28,020 --> 00:07:29,580
many times to get excited.

277
00:07:29,760 --> 00:07:31,400
What I felt was warmth.

278
00:07:31,800 --> 00:07:33,650
Not a heating pad kind of
hot.

279
00:07:33,690 --> 00:07:34,590
More like it was coming

280
00:07:34,590 --> 00:07:36,020
from inside the knee

281
00:07:36,020 --> 00:07:37,290
and spreading around it.

282
00:07:37,340 --> 00:07:38,280
And that was it.

283
00:07:38,320 --> 00:07:39,910
That was the whole
experience.

284
00:07:40,250 --> 00:07:41,700
When I took it off,

285
00:07:41,700 --> 00:07:42,730
I'll be honest,

286
00:07:42,730 --> 00:07:44,370
nothing dramatic had
happened.

287
00:07:44,570 --> 00:07:47,130
And after what that video
said,

288
00:07:47,130 --> 00:07:48,980
that's exactly what I
expected.

289
00:07:49,480 --> 00:07:50,440
What was different

290
00:07:50,440 --> 00:07:51,340
was that for the first

291
00:07:51,340 --> 00:07:52,580
time in two years I'd

292
00:07:52,580 --> 00:07:54,130
done something for my knee

293
00:07:54,130 --> 00:07:55,220
instead of to it.

294
00:07:55,520 --> 00:07:56,560
Twenty minutes,

295
00:07:56,560 --> 00:07:57,670
in my own chair.

296
00:07:57,820 --> 00:07:58,880
No drive,

297
00:07:58,880 --> 00:07:59,870
no copay.

298
00:07:59,910 --> 00:08:01,410
They say twenty minutes.

299
00:08:01,600 --> 00:08:02,660
I did thirty,

300
00:08:02,660 --> 00:08:03,880
twice a day,

301
00:08:03,880 --> 00:08:05,610
lowest setting that first
week.

302
00:08:06,030 --> 00:08:07,580
I put it on the calendar,

303
00:08:07,580 --> 00:08:09,730
once before work, once
after.

304
00:08:10,010 --> 00:08:11,260
The first week,

305
00:08:11,260 --> 00:08:12,020
I couldn't have told

306
00:08:12,020 --> 00:08:13,480
you if anything was
happening.

307
00:08:13,780 --> 00:08:14,670
I tried not to get

308
00:08:14,670 --> 00:08:15,570
my hopes up.

309
00:08:15,830 --> 00:08:16,630
I'd had things help

310
00:08:16,630 --> 00:08:17,950
for a week and then stop.

311
00:08:18,310 --> 00:08:19,410
But somewhere in the
second week

312
00:08:19,410 --> 00:08:20,350
I noticed I'd come down

313
00:08:20,350 --> 00:08:22,010
the stairs without holding
the rail.

314
00:08:22,050 --> 00:08:23,310
I hadn't decided to.

315
00:08:23,380 --> 00:08:24,920
I just did it,

316
00:08:24,920 --> 00:08:27,170
then stopped halfway down
because I realized.

317
00:08:27,310 --> 00:08:28,810
By the end of the fourth
week

318
00:08:28,810 --> 00:08:30,090
I'd slept through the
night

319
00:08:30,090 --> 00:08:31,260
four times running.

320
00:08:31,830 --> 00:08:33,260
I stood at the counter and
finished

321
00:08:33,260 --> 00:08:35,290
making dinner without
looking for the stool.

322
00:08:35,700 --> 00:08:37,100
None of that is dramatic.

323
00:08:37,220 --> 00:08:38,060
All of it was gone

324
00:08:38,060 --> 00:08:39,150
for two years.

325
00:08:39,270 --> 00:08:41,060
A few weeks later my
husband asked

326
00:08:41,060 --> 00:08:41,990
if I wanted to walk

327
00:08:41,990 --> 00:08:43,750
the long way around the
block.

328
00:08:43,900 --> 00:08:44,870
And for the first time

329
00:08:44,870 --> 00:08:45,970
in two years,

330
00:08:45,970 --> 00:08:47,080
I said yes.

331
00:08:47,490 --> 00:08:49,260
I wanted to understand
why,

332
00:08:49,260 --> 00:08:50,700
so I read the whole thing.

333
00:08:51,160 --> 00:08:52,950
It comes down to four
steps.

334
00:08:52,990 --> 00:08:53,650
One.

335
00:08:53,810 --> 00:08:55,570
The tissue around a new
knee can

336
00:08:55,570 --> 00:08:58,350
stay inflamed long after
surgery is over.

337
00:08:58,580 --> 00:08:59,220
Two.

338
00:08:59,540 --> 00:09:01,870
Inflamed tissue holds
extra fluid,

339
00:09:01,870 --> 00:09:02,760
so it takes up more

340
00:09:02,760 --> 00:09:03,920
room than it should.

341
00:09:04,380 --> 00:09:04,990
Three.

342
00:09:05,310 --> 00:09:07,080
There's only so much room
in there.

343
00:09:07,330 --> 00:09:08,720
Bending compresses it.

344
00:09:08,880 --> 00:09:10,410
Straightening pulls it
tight.

345
00:09:10,610 --> 00:09:11,740
That's the squeeze.

346
00:09:12,440 --> 00:09:13,200
Four.

347
00:09:13,590 --> 00:09:15,320
Red and near-infrared
light have been

348
00:09:15,320 --> 00:09:17,580
studied for calming that
inflammation,

349
00:09:17,580 --> 00:09:18,870
so the swelling and the
pressure

350
00:09:18,870 --> 00:09:20,090
can come down with it.

351
00:09:20,300 --> 00:09:21,890
In a randomized trial,

352
00:09:21,890 --> 00:09:23,830
patients given light
therapy after

353
00:09:23,830 --> 00:09:26,030
a knee replacement had
less pain,

354
00:09:26,030 --> 00:09:28,390
less swelling and better
early movement

355
00:09:28,390 --> 00:09:29,600
than those who weren't.

356
00:09:30,620 --> 00:09:32,530
A 2025 review said the
same,

357
00:09:32,530 --> 00:09:34,140
and was clear the evidence

358
00:09:34,140 --> 00:09:35,250
is still limited.

359
00:09:35,400 --> 00:09:36,820
I probably sound like a
broken

360
00:09:36,820 --> 00:09:38,260
record to my family

361
00:09:38,260 --> 00:09:39,710
and the people I work
with.

362
00:09:39,840 --> 00:09:41,570
But after two years of
doing everything

363
00:09:41,570 --> 00:09:43,460
I was told and getting
nowhere,

364
00:09:43,460 --> 00:09:44,640
you have no idea what it's

365
00:09:44,640 --> 00:09:46,220
like to sleep through the
night,

366
00:09:46,220 --> 00:09:47,360
say yes to the walk,

367
00:09:47,360 --> 00:09:48,880
and get my life back.

368
00:09:49,320 --> 00:09:50,550
So take it from me.

369
00:09:50,750 --> 00:09:52,130
Don't spend another year
waiting

370
00:09:52,130 --> 00:09:53,140
for it to settle.

371
00:09:53,280 --> 00:09:55,010
Don't spend two hundred a
session.

372
00:09:55,190 --> 00:09:56,430
More than ten thousand
people

373
00:09:56,430 --> 00:09:57,430
with pain after a knee

374
00:09:57,430 --> 00:09:59,280
replacement have already
tried this.

375
00:09:59,490 --> 00:10:01,080
Some had it worse than I
did.

376
00:10:01,210 --> 00:10:02,330
You can get the KenRelief

377
00:10:02,330 --> 00:10:03,930
wrap from their website,

378
00:10:03,930 --> 00:10:04,920
